{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישמע ה'", :translit "va-yishma Hashem", :gloss "and YHWH heard"} {:he "והאיש משה", :translit "ve-ha-ish Moshe", :gloss "and the man Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'and the man Moses' immediately follows 'and YHWH heard,' implying God alone heard their private speech"}], :frame {:text "Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses privately, so that no one else could hear. The verse states 'And YHWH heard' (Numbers 12:2), and Ba'al HaTurim infers from the immediate juxtaposition of 'and the man Moses' (Numbers 12:3) that God alone perceived their words, since they conducted their conversation between themselves.", :sources ["Numbers 12:2" "Numbers 12:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'and the man Moses' immediately follows 'and YHWH heard,' implying God alone heard their private speech", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:31.223696491Z", :model "glm-5.2"}